# Every entry is a full fingerprint: commit:path:rule:line. That suppresses
# exactly one occurrence in exactly one commit. No path and no rule is ever
# excluded wholesale, so a real secret in the same file, or the same string
# reintroduced in a later commit, still fails the scan.
#
# Add an entry only with a written classification and the date it was checked.
# An undocumented fingerprint is indistinguishable from a hidden leak.


